ebasic (1.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Calling through a PROPERTY of function-pointer type
    (obj.SomeProp(1, 2), via a plain receiver or This.) - calls the
    getter, then calls its result. Completes the "calling through a
    stored function pointer" family of features (DIM'd variable,
    parameter, TYPE field, and now PROPERTY).

 -- eBasic contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200

ebasic (1.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Calling through a TYPE field of function-pointer type
    (obj.cb(1, 2), via a plain receiver or This.) - completes the
    "calling through a stored function pointer" feature from 1.6.0.
    Again needed no Codegen changes, only Sema. A function-pointer-
    typed PROPERTY is explicitly rejected with a clear diagnostic
    rather than silently mishandled.

 -- eBasic contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0200

ebasic (1.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Calling through a stored function pointer (cb(1, 2)), including
    through a function-pointer parameter inside a higher-order FUNCTION -
    turned out to need no Codegen changes at all, only Sema.
  * Stdcall on a plain eBasic-defined SUB/FUNCTION - @ProcName can now
    target real Win32 Stdcall callback APIs (EnumWindows, SetTimer) on
    32-bit x86. Verified live against real cl.exe as well as g++.

 -- eBasic contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 21:10:00 +0200

ebasic (1.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Typed function-pointer parameters in EXTERN/DECLARE - @ProcName can
    now produce a real, structurally-checked function-pointer type
    (SUB|FUNCTION [Cdecl|Stdcall] ([ByVal] AS Type, ...) [AS ReturnType])
    instead of always degrading to ANY PTR, enabling clean interop with
    C APIs taking typed callbacks (qsort, atexit, EnumWindows, GLib
    signal handlers, SQLite callbacks).
  * Real MSVC precompiled-header rule - cl.exe now gets the same PCH
    speedup g++ already had, verified live against real cl.exe.

 -- eBasic contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 20:15:00 +0200

ebasic (1.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * WinUI3 shim example (examples/winui3_shim/) - a hand-written
    C++/WinRT Windows App SDK application driven by a real eBasic
    program via ShellExecuteA (Stdcall/EXTERN), demonstrating the
    recommended pattern from the MSVC/WinUI3 feasibility study's
    Phase 3. No compiler behavior changes in this release.

 -- eBasic contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200

ebasic (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Stdcall calling convention on EXTERN/DECLARE - Win32 APIs (User32/
    GDI/...) are always extern "C" __stdcall; Cdecl was previously the
    only calling convention Declare supported.
  * Fix: EBASIC_LIBRARY_PATH (ebpm's own external-library search-path
    env var) now uses ';' instead of ':' as its delimiter - ':' collided
    with a Windows absolute path's own drive-letter colon.

 -- eBasic contributors <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 14:30:24 +0200

ebasic (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * MSVC backend support for ebc (new windows-msvc CMake preset and CI
    job) - ebc now detects cl/clang-cl on -cxx/CXX and switches to
    MSVC-style command-line flags, alongside the existing g++/clang++
    path.

